  bootwright / machine restart
      Restart machines through their management controllers. --name takes a comma-separated
      list, and the command applies to every listed machine at once. Success reports the power
      state the controller proved, not the state that was requested.

  Usage
    bootwright machine restart [flags]

  Command flags
      --force  Cut power instead of asking the operating system to shut down
      --name   Select comma-separated machine names (required)
      --yes    Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright machine restart --context lab --name node
